'''Faction Damage Bonuses''' increase damage done to all enemy types of the corresponding [[Factions|Faction]], including [[Bosses]]. It is calculated as a '''total damage multiplier''' against the faction in question. 

==Mechanics==
Faction Damage Bonuses increase the weapon's raw damage, and is applied a second time to [[Damage over Time]] (DoT) from status effects created by it, known as "double dipping". For complete mechanics see [[Damage over Time#DoT Damage Scaling]].

[[Faction Damage Mods]] exist for {{Faction|Grineer}}, {{Faction|Corpus}}, {{Faction|Infested}}, {{Faction|Orokin}}, and {{Faction|The Murmur}} for each of the 4 main weapon types (Rifle, Shotgun, Pistol and Melee) as well as [[Railjack]] for those applicable, and all factions have a Primed variant. Damage is increased by x1.05 per rank, up to x1.30 for regular mods and x1.55 for Primed ones, with a base mod equip cost of 4 and they all have a {{Pol|Madurai}} polarity. Faction mods against {{Faction|Sentient}} only exist for melee weapons, which have the {{Pol|Umbra}} polarity and a lower damage bonus but enjoys a [[Set Mods|set effect]] when both {{M|Sacrificial Pressure}} and {{M|Sacrificial Steel}} are equipped together. Currently, {{Faction|Anarchs}},{{Faction|Narmer}}, {{Faction|Scaldra}}, {{Faction|Techrot}}, {{Faction|Stalker}}, and {{Faction|Wild}} lack any faction mods.

{{Faction|Grineer}}, {{Faction|Corpus}}, and {{Faction|Infested}} Faction Mods have no effect on their {{Faction|Corrupted}} or {{Faction|Narmer}} counterparts. For example, {{M|Bane of Grineer}} will work on {{E|Lancer}} but not on {{E|Corrupted Lancer}} or {{E|Narmer Lancer}}. Likewise, {{Faction|Infested}} Faction Mods have no effect on {{Faction|Techrot}}.

